 To solve the equation $(2^{x+1})^3\cdot 4^x=8192$, we can start by simplifying the left side of the equation:
\begin{align*}
(2^{x+1})^3\cdot 4^x &= 8192\\
2^{3(x+1)}\cdot 4^x &= 8192\\
2^3\cdot 2^{(x+1)}\cdot 4^x &= 8192\\
8\cdot 2^x\cdot 4^x &= 8192
\end{align*}
Next, we can simplify the expression further:
\begin{align*}
8\cdot 2^x\cdot 4^x &= 8192\\
4\cdot 2^{x+4} &= 8192
\end{align*}
Now, we can divide both sides by 4 to isolate the term with the exponent:
\begin{align*}
4\cdot 2^{x+4} &= 8192\\
2^{x+4} &= 2048
\end{align*}
To solve for $x$, we can take the logarithm base 2 of both sides:
\begin{align*}
2^{x+4} &= 2048\\
\log_2(2^{x+4}) &= \log_2(2048)\\
x + 4 &= \log_2(2048)\\
x + 4 &= 11\\
x &= 7
\end{align*}
The answer is: $$x=7$$

